<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#talmudic-academy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talmudic academy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Talmudic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Talmudic academy, or yeshiva, is an institution for the advanced study of the Talmud and Jewish law. Such academies flourished in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, whose cities became the heartland of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkenazi-jews">Ashkenazi</a> Jewish civilisation. The Commonwealth profile lists them alongside Hasidic mysticism and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yiddish">Yiddish</a> literary culture as traditions that shaped global Jewish identity for centuries.</p></div>
